      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(channels): expose source actor attribution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nGroup-channel messages need a generic way to distinguish the runtime message author from the operator/user represented by the agent session. Without source actor attribution, downstream prompts, tools, and memory adapters can only see channel/session context and may conflate another group participant with the operator. This should be solved as a channel contract, not as a deployment-specific memory backend workaround.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds a generic `SourceActor` inbound context contract for the runtime identity of the message author.\n- Maps Signal sender identity into `SourceActor` without making the contract Signal-specific.\n- Types `SourceActorRole` as `operator | participant | self | system | external`.\n- Documents `SourceActor` as canonical and the flattened `SourceActor*` fields as scalar mirrors for prompt templates.\n- Exports `SourceActorContext` and `SourceActorRole` from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/reply-runtime`.\n\n## Stack\n\nThis is stacked after #96738 and `codex/signal-mention-facts-context`. Until those land, this PR's diff will include its dependencies.\n\n## Production impact\n\nNo behavior change by itself. The change gives prompts, tools, and memory integrations a stable way to distinguish a group participant from the operator/user. Signal direct and group senders are represented as `participant` source actors.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Channel context tests cover generic `SourceActor` projection and object-to-scalar mirror parity.\n- Channel contract helpers now assert `SourceActor` scalar mirrors stay in sync with the canonical structured object.\n- Signal mention-gating tests cover Signal sender identity mapping into the generic context.\n- Plugin SDK runtime mock tests cover `SourceActor*` parity with production inbound context.\n- Focused tests passed:\n  `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/plugin-runtime-mock.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- Plugin SDK API check passed without a baseline hash diff:\n  `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check`\n- Production TypeScript check passed:\n  `pnpm tsgo:prod`\n\n### Redacted Runtime Proof\n\nTemporary local proof harness imported production `buildChannelInboundEventContext` and printed the emitted prompt context on PR head `5fab61f873`. The proof preserves the emitted source-actor shape while replacing all Signal identifiers, group identifiers, participant names, phone numbers, UUIDs, and message bodies with placeholders.\n\n```console\n$ node --import tsx --input-type=module -e '<redacted proof harness>'\nruntime-proof:environment\n{\n  \"pr\": 96863,\n  \"repo\": \"openclaw/openclaw\",\n  \"head\": \"5fab61f873\",\n  \"node\": \"v26.3.0\"\n}\nruntime-proof:#96863 source actor fields emitted by prompt context\n{\n  \"SourceActor\": {\n    \"id\": \"signal:<redacted-phone>\",\n    \"peerId\": \"signal:<redacted-uuid>\",\n    \"displayName\": \"<redacted-display-name>\",\n    \"role\": \"participant\",\n    \"context\": \"signal-group:<redacted>\"\n  },\n  \"SourceActorId\": \"signal:<redacted-phone>\",\n  \"SourceActorPeerId\": \"signal:<redacted-uuid>\",\n  \"SourceActorDisplayName\": \"<redacted-display-name>\",\n  \"SourceActorRole\": \"participant\",\n  \"SourceActorContext\": \"signal-group:<redacted>\",\n  \"scalarMirrorMatches\": {\n    \"id\": true,\n    \"peerId\": true,\n    \"displayName\": true,\n    \"role\": true,\n    \"context\": true\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Operational Signal group evidence (2026-06-26)\n\nA private Signal group smoke was run after a production config hotfix that kept the group-bound agent responding without changing Docker permissions. The private runtime intentionally stayed on its deployed OpenClaw release instead of being advanced to this PR stack today; the facts below are operational evidence for the real Signal group route, not an additional claim that this PR head is live-deployed.\n\nSanitized facts:\n\n- `openclaw config validate` against `/run/user/1000/openclaw/openclaw.json`: `valid=true`, exit `0`.\n- `openclaw-gateway.service`: `active/running`, `NRestarts=0`.\n- A native Signal mention from a group participant produced an outbound group reply; the journal recorded `delivered reply to group` at `2026-06-26T13:03:19+02:00`.\n- Latest group-bound Signal session metadata for the private family agent: `systemSent=true`, `abortedLastRun=false`.\n- Journal after the smoke: `Failed to inspect sandbox image` count `0`.\n\nDeployment note: the private runtime is not being upgraded to this stack today because that would mix the PR validation with an unrelated Docker sandbox repair. The long-term Docker/rootless sandbox fix is being tracked separately.\n## Tests\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/plugin-runtime-mock.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts`\n- `pnpm plugin-sdk:api:check`\n- `pnpm tsgo:prod`\n\n### Evidence update\n\nCurrent-head proof on `codex/source-actor-context-contract` (`4647951f5b`):\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/channels/inbound-event/context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts src/plugin-sdk/test-helpers/plugin-runtime-mock.test.ts\n[test] passed 3 Vitest shards in 28.32s\n\n$ node --max-old-space-size=8192 --import tsx scripts/generate-plugin-sdk-api-baseline.ts --check\nOK docs/.generated/plugin-sdk-api-baseline.sha256\n\n$ git diff --check\n# passed with no output\n```\n\nGitHub state after the current-head push:\n\n- `mergeStateStatus=CLEAN`\n- `Real behavior proof=SUCCESS`\n- `git diff --check` clean locally before push\n\nInspectable assertions covered:\n\n- `SourceActor` is the canonical attribution object.\n- `SourceActorId`, `SourceActorPeerId`, `SourceActorDisplayName`,\n  `SourceActorRole`, and `SourceActorContext` mirror the canonical object.\n- The plugin SDK runtime mock now mirrors both the canonical object and the scalar fields.\n- The stack inherits #96862's `WasMentioned` compatibility fix: delivered Signal turns\n  keep `WasMentioned` as the effective mention-gating result.\n- The stack inherits #96862's canonical mention-policy shape: `GroupRequireMention`,\n  not a duplicate `RequireMention` alias.\n- The plugin SDK runtime mock mirrors `MentionShouldSkip`.\n- `SourceActor.role` is constrained to the typed role set:\n  `operator`, `participant`, `self`, `system`, `external`.\n- Type docs state that display names and peer ids are channel-supplied metadata,\n  not trusted authorization facts.\n\nNo private Signal identifiers, phone numbers, participant names, or group ids are used in this proof.\n",
